  "specific_guards": [
    {
      "id": "G-drag-rigid",
      "basis": "UI window open before selected birth,1110 physical rows,complete/no failure/no overflow/no dropped; zero Item entry globally and for matched39. Exact instrumented Item hooks precede global_position/rotation/direct Util.rng branches. Therefore those branches did not execute within the recorded fixed window; not inferred merely from initialfalse."
    },
    {
      "id": "G-focus",
      "basis": "39 initialfocus/hovered/draggedfalse; original Item positive focus write is gainFocus\u2192respondToHover, whose entry hook is unconditional. No selected respondToHover/End entry. Exact direct external .focus assignment search returned none; only nonselected Gem declares gainFocus/loseFocus overrides. Selected fixed no-gem domain is inherited from accepted fixture. No new generic reflection/native mutation claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "G-controller",
      "basis": "roles using_controller=false; sink checks inputdisabled/pickingfalse/controllerfalse on every physics+idle clock signal and each UI write; failedfalse complete window. Original Game positive usingController assignment is in _input; versionmatched Viewport._vp_input returns when disable_input. Ordinary baseline GDScript search found no set_disable_input or direct viewport.input calls. Not a claim about hostile synthetic native dispatch."
    },
    {
      "id": "G-residual",
      "basis": "Game.recalculateCursor/getCursorType/cursor setters write only cursor fields/textures/custom cursor. Software Cursor script updates sprite/position; its deferred show is presentation. Item.updateShadow/lock rotation and sprite color are display operations. Noncombat affected-highlight branch needs a focus/dragged item; disabled input/zero Item hover/drag branch plus ordinary fixed-case setup must be assessed as this finite guard, not fullGUI reproduction."
    },
    {
      "id": "G-derived-Bag",
      "basis": "Item subclasses must not be silently assumed to replace base notifications: versionmatched Node.cpp54\u201365 uses call_multilevel for process/physics. Selected Bag._process104\u2013112 is a dragged-only tilemap appearance branch. It adds no selected primitive/business effect under the same drag guard. Existing accepted ordinaryG02 script-dispatch domain applies; no kernel modifications."
    }
  ],
